Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:38:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add density-matrix propagation with dephasing

Each k point carries a 2x2 density matrix. The coherent step is the same SU(2) update as the pure-state propagator, and the coherences decay as exp(-t / T2) with a symmetric split. With T2 = infinity the current matches the pure-state result to 1e-13. Tests check the trace, positivity, the exact free decay of the coherence, time-step convergence and input validation.


